{"contributions":[{"contribution":"Correct generated/hello-world.mjs with a small, bounded change so that `node generated/hello-world.mjs`, run without installing any package, writes exactly `Hello, world!` plus one newline to stdout and exits 0. Change only the greeting text the baseline showed to be wrong (the missing comma). Keep it a plain Node ESM script with no dependencies. Do not modify the tests, source, oracle or contract, which are protected.","dependsOn":[],"evidenceRefs":["task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5","worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/8c825b4d40551911518312b076b03aa3b907a0e7f685880ef11f9cc6075dfd47","result://abiogenesis/b63cfd1dc0bc193ebab9987177c88119d945add00bc62eaf4b955388dc513aea"],"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/construction@5","reason":"The admitted baseline (result b63cfd1d…) shows a real failure of the supplied CLI: stdout was 'Hello world!\n' instead of 'Hello, world!\n', and both supplied tests failed. That observed failure justifies a registered choice different from the measurement, namely a correction in the same lineage, as the witness contract requires. Without the baseline, a repair would have been unobserved. The construction's own report is not acceptance.","supportRefs":["obligation://default-library-witness/revision@5","obligation://default-library-witness/behavior@5","obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5"]},{"contribution":"Measure the corrected current subject again with the two fixed commands, run from the project root: `node generated/hello-world.mjs` and `node --test test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs`. Record the command, args, cwd, environment, exit status, stdout, stderr and pass/fail counts, including any nonzero exit. Write only under execution-evidence. The earlier baseline result stays historical evidence about the old bytes and is not overwritten.","dependsOn":["graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/construction@5"],"evidenceRefs":["task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5","result://abiogenesis/b63cfd1dc0bc193ebab9987177c88119d945add00bc62eaf4b955388dc513aea"],"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/testing@5","reason":"The behavior obligation needs actual current CLI stdout, exit 0, and at least two real passing tests with zero failures, all measured against the corrected bytes. The revision obligation needs the correction's consequence to be observed on the same lineage as the baseline failure.","supportRefs":["obligation://default-library-witness/behavior@5","obligation://default-library-witness/revision@5","obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5"]},{"contribution":"Write specification/project-conformance.md from scratch. It states the Intent, the Product boundary, source-grounded requirements and completion criteria for the minimal Node CLI Hello World traversal. The source surface is generated/hello-world.mjs. The execution proof runs the CLI and observes stdout exactly "Hello, world!\n" with exit status 0. Completion requires the component and UAT tests to execute the real CLI with at least 2 passes and 0 failures. The file contains no source, tests, package files or execution plans.","dependsOn":[],"evidenceRefs":["task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5","worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/8c825b4d40551911518312b076b03aa3b907a0e7f685880ef11f9cc6075dfd47"],"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/specification@5","reason":"The conformance asset is absent and must be authored with real content. It is the authority for the implementation design. The baseline does not change its meaning.","supportRefs":["obligation://default-library-witness/conformance@5","obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5"]},{"contribution":"Write three files from scratch. (1) design/implementation-design.md: takes the conformance asset as authority; defines a minimal Node CLI at generated/hello-world.mjs that prints exactly "Hello, world!" plus one newline; names test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs and test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs as the verification surfaces. (2) design/test-design.md: component and UAT checks that spawn node generated/hello-world.mjs, assert status 0, and assert stdout exactly "Hello, world!\n", matching the actual supplied tests. (3) test-execution-plan.json: command node, args ["--test","test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs","test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs"], expectedTestPassCount >= 2, expectedStdoutMatch including a stable zero-failure fragment such as fail 0, and assertedReturnValue "Hello, world!". The plan must agree with the fixed commands but does not control execution.","dependsOn":["graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/specification@5"],"evidenceRefs":["task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5","worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/8c825b4d40551911518312b076b03aa3b907a0e7f685880ef11f9cc6075dfd47","result://abiogenesis/b63cfd1dc0bc193ebab9987177c88119d945add00bc62eaf4b955388dc513aea"],"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/design@5","reason":"All three assets are absent. The implementation design must follow the actual conformance asset. The test design and plan must match the supplied verifiers, which the baseline showed to be real CLI-executing checks, and the fixed prospective commands.","supportRefs":["obligation://default-library-witness/implementation-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/test-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/execution-plan@5","obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5"]},{"contribution":"A read-only, independent assessment of the complete original outcome. It uses the exact current candidate, the original source, the oracle rubric, the witness contract and the current admitted execution evidence. It covers:
- the content of the authored conformance, implementation design, test design and plan, and how they correspond to the source and to each other;
- whether the verifiers are adequate;
- whether the plan agrees with the fixed commands;
- the current CLI's stdout and exit status, and the test pass/fail counts;
- the causal link from the historical baseline failure to the correction.
Unmet and indeterminate criteria are kept.","dependsOn":["graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/testing@5","graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/specification@5","graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/design@5","graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/construction@5"],"evidenceRefs":["task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5","result://abiogenesis/b63cfd1dc0bc193ebab9987177c88119d945add00bc62eaf4b955388dc513aea"],"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/uat@5","reason":"Parent completion requires an independent semantic assessment of current admitted evidence for all seven obligations. The assessor must be distinct from the authors and from the measurement producer.","supportRefs":["obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5","obligation://default-library-witness/conformance@5","obligation://default-library-witness/implementation-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/test-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/execution-plan@5","obligation://default-library-witness/behavior@5","obligation://default-library-witness/revision@5"]}],"gaps":[],"interpretation":"The baseline measurement is now recorded (result b63cfd1d…). It was taken against the supplied 29-byte CLI, sha256:647697a5…. Command 0 (`node generated/hello-world.mjs`) exited 0 and printed `Hello world!\n` (13 bytes), which lacks the comma the original requires in `Hello, world!\n`. Command 1 (`node --test` on the component and UAT files) exited 1: 2 tests ran, 0 passed, 2 failed. Both failures are strictEqual stdout assertions at line 8 of each test (actual 'Hello world!\n', expected 'Hello, world!\n'). The status assertions at line 7 passed. This matches the declared nonzero result for command 1 and supplies the admitted baseline failure the revision obligation needs. It also shows that both supplied tests really spawn and check the current CLI, so they are working verifiers. The defect is limited to the stdout text; the exit status is already correct. The failure belongs to the old bytes and stays historical evidence. Once the CLI is corrected, only claims that depend on those bytes still being current become stale. All authored assets are still absent. All seven obligations remain open. No current-subject behavior evidence or independent assessment exists yet.","nextEvidenceRefs":["task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5","worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/8c825b4d40551911518312b076b03aa3b907a0e7f685880ef11f9cc6075dfd47","result://abiogenesis/b63cfd1dc0bc193ebab9987177c88119d945add00bc62eaf4b955388dc513aea"],"nextGraphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/construction@5","nextReason":"The baseline failure is now admitted and pins the defect to the stdout text alone: 'Hello world!\n' was printed instead of 'Hello, world!\n', while exit 0 was already correct. That makes the bounded CLI correction the justified, different registered choice the contract requires. Fixing the one broken point in the runnable path first lets the next measurement settle the behavior and revision obligations against the corrected bytes. Specification and design can follow; they do not depend on these CLI bytes.","requirementProposals":[],"revisionEvidenceRefs":["result://abiogenesis/b63cfd1dc0bc193ebab9987177c88119d945add00bc62eaf4b955388dc513aea","result://abiogenesis/1a1eb2bc65561cf7a3f9035b5208eb549b6a2d0e5d06375e85b1de60251b1771"],"revisionReason":"The previous judgment selected testing as a baseline with no prerequisites. That baseline has now run and been admitted (result b63cfd1d…). Construction's dependency on testing in this mapping is replaced by an evidence reference to that completed result. The testing row now means re-measuring the corrected current subject, so it depends on construction. The baseline stays historical evidence about the old bytes. The specification, design and UAT rows are kept. UAT's dependency on testing now points at the re-measurement.","subjectEvidenceRef":null}

